nl80211_create_bridge(): don't take the OVS path when OVS userspace
isn't there, and don't report success when creating the OVS bridge
failed.

Two problems, one of which silently breaks every VAP-to-bridge
enslavement on this platform.

1. The OVS branch is gated on access(OVS_MODULE, F_OK), i.e. on
   /sys/module/openvswitch existing -- the *kernel module*. That says
   nothing about whether this system's bridges are OVS bridges, and
   inside an LXD container it isn't even this system's property: /sys is
   the host's, so a module the host loaded for something else entirely
   makes every container take the OVS path. On the lab host rev150
   openvswitch is loaded (lsmod shows 6 users, none of them ours) and
   both RDK-B containers therefore saw /sys/module/openvswitch despite
   shipping no running ovsdb-server. Also require ovs-vsctl's own
   compiled-in default socket to exist, which is what it will actually
   try to connect to; when OVS genuinely is in use both are true and
   behavior is unchanged.

2. In the branch that creates the bridge, ovs_add_br() failing is not
   handled at all:

       if (ovs_add_br(br_name) == 0) {
           if (ovs_br_add_if(br_name, if_name) != 0) { ...; return -1; }
       }
       /* falls through */
       wifi_hal_dbg_print("... ovs bridge mapping ... is created\n");
       return 0;

   so a failed ovs_add_br() skips the inner block, falls through to the
   "is created" log and returns success having done nothing. Every other
   failure in this function returns -1; this one is the exception.

Together these produced a completely silent failure. wifi_hal logged

  nl80211_create_bridge:4400 ovs bridge mapping for bridge:brlan0, interface:wifi1.3 is created
  wifi_hal_configure_sta_4addr_to_bridge:9137: Sta wifi1.3 interface added successfully to bridge:brlan0

while /sys/class/net/brlan0/brif/ contained only eth1_virt_end -- the
mesh backhaul STA was never enslaved, so the EasyMesh leaf had no data
path to the controller at all. Its AP-Autoconfiguration Search frames
left the STA (33 seen on the leaf's own interface) and died on the
isolated bridge; zero arrived at the controller, which therefore never
answered and no fronthaul VAP was ever configured. Fixing the gate lets
control reach the existing Linux-bridge netlink path further down, which
is what this platform actually needs; fixing the fall-through means a
real OVS failure is reported instead of masked.

Not hwsim-specific -- the fall-through is a plain bug, and the module
-vs-userspace confusion affects any containerized or module-loaded-but
-unused system -- so neither part is gated.

---
 wifi_hal_nl80211.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
@@ -84,6 +84,9 @@
 
 #define AP_UNABLE_TO_HANDLE_ADDITIONAL_ASSOCIATIONS 17
 #define OVS_MODULE "/sys/module/openvswitch"
+/* ovs-vsctl's compiled-in default database socket. Presence of the kernel module
+ * alone does not mean this system's bridges are OVS bridges -- see nl80211_create_bridge(). */
+#define OVS_DB_SOCK "/var/run/openvswitch/db.sock"
 #define ONEWIFI_TESTSUITE_TMPFILE "/tmp/onewifi_testsuite_configured"
 #define KEY_MGMT_SAE_EXT 67108864
 #define MAX_MBSSID_INTERFACES 8
@@ -4373,7 +4376,8 @@
         br_name, if_name, is_hotspot_interface, is_lnf_psk_interface, is_mdu_enabled,
         (vap_cfg != NULL)? vap_cfg->vap_name: "NULL");
 
-    if (access(OVS_MODULE, F_OK) == 0 && !is_hotspot_interface && !(is_lnf_psk_interface && is_mdu_enabled)) {
+    if (access(OVS_MODULE, F_OK) == 0 && access(OVS_DB_SOCK, F_OK) == 0 &&
+        !is_hotspot_interface && !(is_lnf_psk_interface && is_mdu_enabled)) {
         if (ovs_if_get_br(ovs_brname, if_name) == 0) {
             if (strcmp(br_name, ovs_brname) != 0) {
                 wifi_hal_dbg_print("%s:%d mismatch\n",  __func__, __LINE__);
@@ -4394,6 +4398,9 @@
                         wifi_hal_error_print("%s:%d adding interface:%s to bridge:%s failed\n",  __func__, __LINE__, if_name, br_name);
                         return -1;
                     }
+                } else {
+                    wifi_hal_error_print("%s:%d creating ovs bridge:%s for interface:%s failed\n",  __func__, __LINE__, br_name, if_name);
+                    return -1;
                 }
             }
         }
